senses.gloss:
√añj or aj (anákti, aṅkté; ānáñja, ānajé
[788]; ā́ñjīt; aktá; aktvā́; -áñjya, -ájya).
 —1. smear; anoint;
 —2. adorn. [cf. aktu:
cf. Lat. ungo, ‘anoint.’]
+ ā, anoint.
+ vi,
 —1. anoint;
 —2. adorn; and so, bring
to notice; vyàkta: adorned, fair; manifest;
 --caus. make clear or manifest.
+ sam,
 —1. anoint;
 —2. adorn;
 —3. unite
by anointing, 89^19;
 —4. generalized, unite
with, take to one's self (e. g. food), 88^10.
